      "title": "Can Centene Sustain Its Turnaround Amid Membership Pressure?",
      "summary": "Centene Corporation reported Q2 2026 adjusted EPS of $2.51, marking a significant recovery from a loss a year prior, driven by improved medical cost trends and better execution. The company expects Medicaid membership to decline 8%-9% in 2026, but profitability improvements in Marketplace and Medicare segments, combined with higher Medicaid rates and cost initiatives, support continued recovery. CNC reaffirmed its 2026 adjusted EPS guidance above $4.80.",
